erone level, ln SHBG level, and SHBG-bound testosterone level.</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ehp-116-1635"><label>b</label><p>Significant with further adjustment for Great Lakes fish meals or sport fish meals in the last year (<italic>r</italic> = &#x02212;0.12, <italic>p</italic> = 0.04).</p></fn><fn id="tfn5-ehp-116-1635"><label>c</label><p>Borderline significant (0.05 &#x0003c; <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.10) with further adjustment for HA1c, ln SHBG, SHBG-bound testosterone, or ln DDE</p></fn><fn id="tfn6-ehp-116-1635"><label>d</label><p>Borderline significant (0.05 &#x0003c; <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.10) with further adjustment for alcohol consumption, Great Lakes fish meals in the last year, ln SHBG, or SHBG-bound testosterone.</p></fn><fn id="tfn7-ehp-116-1635"><label>e</label><p>Adjusted for urinary creatinine.</p></fn><fn id="tfn8-ehp-116-1635"><label>f</label><p>Significant with further adjustment for testosterone (<italic>r</italic> = &#x02212;0.12, <italic>p</italic> = 0.05).</p></fn><fn id="tfn9-ehp-116-1635"><label>g</label><p>Significant after exclusion of two extreme outliers for T<sub>4</sub>-bound albumin (<italic>r</italic> = 0.13, <italic>p</italic> = 0.03).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t3-ehp-116-1635" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Associations of hormones with BDE-47, BDE-99, BDE-100, and BDE-153 tertiles.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Hormone</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Measure</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BDE-47</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BDE-99</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BDE-100</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BDE-153</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ln TSH (&#x003bc;IU/mL)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x003b2; for tertile 2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn10-ehp-116-1635">a</xref><